<title>PERU: Peru's July sugar output dips 21.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's July sugar output dips 21.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's sugar production fell 21.7 percent in July to 456,832 tonnes, compared to the same month last year, Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The ministry's monthly report added that sugar output for the first seven months was off 5.9 percent at 3.035 million tonnes from the same period last year.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 6.325 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports of sugar rose 48.1 percent in July to 16,190 tonnes, worth $8.274 million. In the first seven months, imports rose 12.7 percent to 178,292 tonnes, worth $59.911 million.</p>
<p>Exports of sugar rose 19.4 percent in July to 16,883 tonnes, worth $38.6 million, while exports in the first seven months grew 41 percent to 53,175 tonnes worth $118.2 million.</p>
<p>--Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
